text:
maria: Quick check — we're seeing growing TIME_WAIT sockets from the .NET SDK when clients stream long responses. Pattern looks like SDK creates/ disposes HttpClient per call and we have a Polly retry handler on top. Anyone triaged this pattern before?

sam: Yep — creating/disposing HttpClient per request is a classic. Use IHttpClientFactory or a long-lived HttpClient. Also tune SocketsHttpHandler.PooledConnectionLifetime and MaxConnectionsPerServer. For streaming, be careful: retries can collide with an in-progress stream. :warning:

ben: We usually register via DI and attach Polly via AddPolicyHandler. Example:

```csharp
services.AddHttpClient("redwood", client => {
  client.BaseAddress = new Uri("https://api.redwood.dev");
})
.ConfigurePrimaryHttpMessageHandler(() => new SocketsHttpHandler {
  PooledConnectionLifetime = TimeSpan.FromMinutes(5),
  MaxConnectionsPerServer = 100
})
.AddPolicyHandler(HttpPolicyExtensions.HandleTransientHttpError()
  .WaitAndRetryAsync(new[] { TimeSpan.FromSeconds(1), TimeSpan.FromSeconds(2) }));
```

This keeps socket reuse and lets the handler reuse connections.

jen: Quick follow — if we call ReadAsStreamAsync and the body is large/long-lived, Polly could trigger a retry while the stream is being consumed. That causes half-read bodies / cancelled reads. Any recommended pattern for streaming endpoints?

sam: Two approaches: 1) Disable automatic retries for streaming endpoints (use a separate named client or policy) — simplest. 2) If you must retry, only retry before the body is consumed (i.e., on failures that happen before reading the response stream). Implement a custom policy that inspects whether the response has started streaming (response.Content.Headers.ContentLength or a flag) and only retries when safe. In practice we avoid transparent retries for live streaming and instead provide resumable offsets/tokens.

rohit: FWIW we had this exact bug in SDK v1.3 — we were constructing HttpClient per call and our DelegatingHandler attempted to resend the request on transient 5xx, which re-sent the request while the app was reading the original stream. PR #452 switches to IHttpClientFactory, fixes handler logic, and adds a NoAutoRetry flag for streaming endpoints. Rolling canary now.

deploy-bot: merged PR #452 into main — staging build 2026-03-15-rc1 :shipit:

maria: Great. Action items: @rohit please land the v1.4 patch (I think that's the PR). @jen can you add streaming-specific integration tests that assert no automatic retries while ReadAsStreamAsync is in-progress? @ben can you add the AddHttpClient example to the SDK docs under "connection pooling and streaming"? I'll open a tracking issue and add the checklist. Thanks all :thumbsup:
